[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/banner.jpg[/img]

[h1]Dazed Core[/h1]
[b]The shared foundation of the Dazed mod suite for Build 42.[/b]
It does nothing on its own. Every Dazed mod loads it first.

[table]
[tr][td][b]Game version[/b][/td][td]Build 42 only (42.0+)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Multiplayer[/b][/td][td]Built for it, server is the authority. Not yet tested on a dedicated server, reports welcome[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Add mid-save[/b][/td][td]Yes[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Load order[/b][/td][td]Before every other Dazed mod (they require it automatically)[/td][/tr]
[tr][td][b]Mod ID[/b][/td][td]DazedCore[/td][/tr]
[/table]

[hr][/hr]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/h-what.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/core.png[/img]
You will never open Dazed Core directly, but you will feel it in every Dazed mod:

[list]
[*][b]Heavy parts:[/b] anything over 30 kg (big tanks, solar arrays, controllers) is carried as parts, (1/2) and (2/2), just like a vanilla bed or shelving. Placing needs every part on you.
[*][b]Building Picker:[/b] click houses, basements or structures you built yourself to serve them with power or water. Green is served, yellow adds, blue removes, red is out of reach.
[*][b]One sandbox preset:[/b] Custom, Easy, Standard, Realistic or Hardcore on the Dazed Core sandbox page sets the options of Power, Plumbing, Climate and Essentials at once.
[*][b]Dazed Mod Suite Guide:[/b] a book button at the foot of the left sidebar opens an in-game guide, with tabs for Basics, Power, Plumbing, Butchery, Cooking and Dank when those mods are on.
[*][b]Shared options page:[/b] every Dazed tick box and key lives under one "Dazed Core" entry in the Mods options tab.
[*][b]Temperatures:[/b] one setting (game setting, Celsius or Fahrenheit) that Climate, Dank, the EVs and the thermometer all follow.
[*][b]Plays nice:[/b] a Dazed feature steps aside when another mod you run already does the same job.
[*][b]Debug spawn:[/b] in debug mode or for server staff, a "Dazed debug" right-click menu spawns a mod's whole item set for testing.
[*][b]Server sync:[/b] the server is the authority, clients stay in step, and a line above your head tells you why something was refused.
[/list]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/picker.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/settings.png[/img]

[hr][/hr]

[h2]The Dazed suite[/h2]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/suite.png[/img]
[list]
[*][b]Dazed Power[/b]: solar, wind, steam and gas generators feeding battery banks, with a controller and cabled buildings
[*][b]Dazed Power: Electric Vehicles[/b]: homemade 1993 electric vehicles built from car batteries and charged from your Power system
[*][b]Dazed Plumbing[/b]: tanks, pipes, pumps, wells, rain collection, purifiers and a water main that brings a whole house back to life
[*][b]Dazed Dank[/b]: realistic cannabis growing: strains, grow rooms, hydro, drying, curing and smoking
[*][b]Dazed Dank: Garden Crops[/b]: grow vanilla crops in Dank's grow bags and hydro
[*][b]Dazed Butchery[/b]: pick a primal from the carcass and trace every cut yourself; hidden grades, field dressing, dry-aging
[*][b]Dazed Cooking[/b]: every cut has a best method and a best doneness; cook it right and your survivor feels it
[*][b]Dazed Climate[/b]: a temperature overhaul: real winters, rooms that hold heat, frost on crops, row tunnels and freezing pipes
[*][b]Dazed Essentials[/b]: common-sense quality of life, every feature a sandbox switch
[/list]

[hr][/hr]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/h-authors.png[/img]
Dazed Core is a library other mods can build on: a power registry (register a provider or a load and ask [i]isPowered(obj)[/i] about any object), building and reach resolution, synced ModData tables, a client-to-authority request layer with rate limits, mod detection so features can yield to another mod, schema migration, one temperature lookup for every mod, 20 shared part tags (motors, compressors, copper tubing, wiring harnesses and more) that any Dazed recipe can name, a debug spawn menu mods add item sets to, and a shared Error Magnifier report. Full API notes and headless tests are in the GitHub repo.

[url=https://github.com/Dazedgenie/DazedCore]Source on GitHub[/url]

[hr][/hr]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/h-compat.png[/img]
[list]
[*]Build 42 only. There is no Build 41 version and there will not be one.
[*]Safe to add to an existing save. Removing it will break any Dazed mod that depends on it.
[*]Multiplayer is written for a dedicated server but has not been tested on one yet. Multiplayer bugs are the ones I most want to hear about.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Dazedgenie/Dazed-Workshop/main/Core/images/h-help.png[/img]
Post in the Discussions tab or open an issue on GitHub. Please include your game version, the Dazed mods you run, and your console.txt if there is an error.

